# DRIVE Firebase Rules

- Before Firebase work, read `docs/05-technical-architecture.md` and `docs/06-firestore-schema.md`.
- Do not add Firebase code until the user explicitly requests Firebase implementation.
- Keep Firebase access inside repositories or services. Screens and presentational components must not read or write Firestore or Storage directly.
- Treat PM5 photos as private squad training evidence. Do not add public sharing or galleries.
- Athletes may submit their own evidence, but must not verify submissions or write rewards directly.
- Coaches may verify or reject submissions only for squads they are authorised to coach.
- Reward records must be created only after coach verification and should reference the verified submission.
- Do not let client UI write arbitrary XP, attributes, badges, River Map progress, Boathouse progress, or squad mission progress.
- Once the app exists, run typecheck and lint after Firebase changes and report the result.
